# APRly billing vs GHL (locked facts)

Do **not** mention monthly subscription ($19.99/mo) when discussing GHL integration,
E1–E8, Cliff letters, or integration summaries. It is **not relevant**.

## Product billing (actual code)

- **Only payment that matters for GHL and partner send:** one-time **$39 audit** (`users.paidAuditAt`).
- **E3** fires on first successful $39 audit payment (`finalizeAuditCheckoutIfNeeded` → `ghlSyncPaidAudit`).
- **Gate for send to partner:** `resolveHasPaidAccess` = `paidAuditAt != null` ([`subscription-status.ts`](artifacts/api-server/src/lib/subscription-status.ts)).
- Checkout path: `POST /me/audit-checkout` (not a recurring subscription product for this flow).

## Naming legacy

- UI/API may still say `subscriptionActive` / `hasActiveSubscription` — that maps to **paid audit ($39)**, not a monthly plan.
- `resolveSubscriptionActive` is a **deprecated alias** of `resolveHasPaidAccess`.

## GHL implications

- `has_paid_audit` custom field = user paid the **$39 audit**.
- E2 nurture «pay $39» refers to this one-time audit only.
- **No GHL event** exists or is planned for monthly billing — do not document otherwise.
